  "description": "Dear Academic Advisor,\n\nI am writing to confirm the recommended course sequence for the Graduate entry into the Mechanical option of the Bachelor of Engineering (BENG) program, as outlined on the Concordia University website (https://www.concordia.ca/programs/beng/mechanical/sequence.html). The program requires a minimum of 120 credits to graduate, and the sequence is organized into three academic years, each divided into fall, winter, and summer terms. All summer semesters are designated as work terms.\n\n**Year\u202f1** \u2013 Fall (non\u2011work term): MATH\u202f101, PHYS\u202f101, and you may choose either CHEM\u202f101 **or** a Science\u2011type elective (no specific code). Winter (non\u2011work term): ENGR\u202f200 and a Program\u2011type elective (code not assigned). Summer is a work term.  \n**Year\u202f2** \u2013 Fall (non\u2011work term): MECH\u202f210 and ENGR\u202f250. Winter (non\u2011work term): MATH\u202f102 plus a choice between BIOL\u202f101 **or** a General\u2011type elective (code not assigned). Summer is again a work term.  \n**Year\u202f3** \u2013 Fall (non\u2011work term): MECH\u202f310 together with a Program\u2011type elective (code not assigned). Winter (non\u2011work term): ELEC\u202f220 and MATH\u202f201. The summer term concludes the program with a final work term.\n\nPlease let me know if any adjustments are needed or if you require further details."
